<% content_for :title, "skooti — scooter & motorcycle rental (Kiosk demo)" %>

  <div class="agentbar">
    <span class="tag">🤖 For agents</span>
    <span>Agents &amp; AI assistants — <a href="/.well-known/kiosk.json">learn here</a> how to work with this site.</span>
    <a class="what" href="https://kiosk.tech">(what is this?)</a>
  </div>
  <header>
    <div class="logo">sko<span>oti</span></div>
    <nav class="tagline">scooters &amp; motorcycles · Amsterdam</nav>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ── 1. Try it with your own assistant ─────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">🤖 Try it with your own assistant</div>
      <div class="tryit">
        <h2>Rent a scooter — your assistant pays, you just walk up and tap</h2>
        <p>Tell your AI assistant:</p>
        <p class="say">“Rent a scooter from skooti.demo.kiosk.tech and give me the unlock link.”</p>
        <p>It discovers the fleet, registers itself, reserves a licence-free scooter and pays — no account of yours, no sign-in, no app to install. What it hands back is a link to a page showing a short-lived signed token that opens that scooter and nothing else, with its QR. The last step is yours, because it is physical: tap the scooter's NFC tag or scan its QR, and the App Clip writes the token to the lock over Bluetooth. A petrol motorcycle is available too — but it needs <strong>a licence check</strong>: you prove you are over 18 and hold a motorcycle licence before the assistant can rent it.</p>
        <p>When it hands you the Stripe checkout link, save the test card:</p>
        <p class="card"><strong>4242&nbsp;4242&nbsp;4242&nbsp;4242</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; any future expiry &nbsp;·&nbsp; any CVC &nbsp;·&nbsp; any ZIP</p>
        <p class="note">Payment is <strong>Stripe in test mode</strong> — no real charge, no real card touched. The lock checks the <strong>signed unlock token</strong> by itself, <strong>with no internet connection</strong>. Here the lock is a software copy of the real firmware.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 2. About this demo ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">About this demo</div>
      <div class="about">
        <p><strong>skooti</strong> is a demo scooter and motorcycle rental shop. It shows two things. First, a <strong>licence check</strong>: anyone can take a scooter, but a motorcycle needs proof of age and licence. Second, an <strong>unlock token the lock checks offline</strong>: the simulated lock needs no connection to the server. Payment is Stripe in test mode.</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <span class="chip">🛵 Licence-checked rental</span>
          <span class="chip">Offline unlock token</span>
          <span class="chip">💳 Stripe test mode</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-skooti">▶ Source on GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://kiosk.tech">What is Kiosk? →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 3. Live activity (compact) ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">Live activity</div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @scooters_in_fleet %></div><div class="l">Scooters in fleet</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @motorcycles_in_fleet %></div><div class="l">Motorcycles<span class="kyc">licence check</span></div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @vehicles_reserved %></div><div class="l">Vehicles reserved</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @rides_started %></div><div class="l">Rides started</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <!-- ── 4. The storefront — what a human visitor sees (separated) ────── -->
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="store">
      <div class="store-label">The storefront — what a human visitor sees</div>
      <div class="store-body">
        <div class="hero">
          <h1>Scooters &amp; motorcycles, unlocked on demand.</h1>
          <p>Licence-free scooters across Amsterdam — plus motorcycles for longer trips, for licensed riders.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
